TYPES.md §1, §9.1, §10.2, §13.1: a keyed list whose key field's type is in error (an alias referring to itself, E3021) stays keyed: no E3012 for the key, no E2103 for a ref to its record, no E3003 for a keyed-list method.
-- a/a.canon --
package a

/// A name.
type Ident = Ident

/// A column.
record Col {
  /// Its name.
  name: Ident
}

/// Every column, by name.
let cols: [Col] keyed by name = []

/// A use of a column.
record Use {
  /// The column.
  col: ref Col
}

/// The columns, as a list.
fn all() -> [Col] { return cols.values() }
-- findings.txt --
error[E3021]  a/a.canon:4:6
  type alias Ident refers to itself

